<title>USA: Nebraska fed cattle bid $112, no trade-feedlots.</title>
<headline>Nebraska fed cattle bid $112, no trade-feedlots.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nebraska feedlot managers passed bids of $112.00 per cwt on a dressed basis and $69.00 on a live basis Tuesday, market sources said.</p>
<p>Packer inquiry was light and no trading was reported early Tuesday, they said.</p>
<p>Feedlots were pricing cattle from $114.00 to $115.00 on a dressed basis and mostly $71.00 on a live basis, with a few offers of $72.00.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
</text>
